  "id": "ENT097",
  "title": "The Plant-Watering Calendar Duel",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "everyday microdramas",
  "premise": "Two roommates each think the other forgot to water a decorative paper plant and add blue paper droplets to its pot. The absurd droplet pile reveals the duplicated effort; they put one reversible DONE card beside the pot and take turns flipping it as part of a pretend care routine.",
  "hook": "We both remembered. That is the problem.",
  "visible_action": "Blue paper droplets accumulate; pot bulges with confetti; roommates compare calendars; one two-sided card flips and droplets stop doubling.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Make a shared task’s status visible to both people.",
  "gate": "Use a clearly artificial plant and paper water; no real plant watering frequency or care advice.",
